<title>ANGOLA: Land mine injures four peacekeepers in Angola.</title>
<headline>Land mine injures four peacekeepers in Angola.</headline>
<dateline>LUANDA 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four Brazilian members of the U.N. peacekeeping force in Angola were wounded on Sunday when their vehicle hit a landmine in the central province of Bie, the state news agency Angop said on Monday.</p>
<p>About 6,500 U.N. peacekeepers are monitoring a peace accord signed in November 1994 between the Angolan government and the UNITA opposition. The two sides were at war since the country's independence in 1975.</p>
</text>
